# See https://help.github.com/articles/ignoring-files/ for more about ignoring files.

# dependencies
/node_modules
/.pnp
.pnp.*
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches
!.yarn/plugins
!.yarn/releases
!.yarn/versions

# testing
/coverage

# next.js
/.next/
/out/

# production
/build

# misc
.DS_Store
*.pem

# debug
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.pnpm-debug.log*

# env files (can opt-in for committing if needed)
.env*

# vercel
.vercel

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Added 2026-09-15, per Vignesh asking "is the current folder nice?" before
# pushing to GitHub. Two real problems found sitting in C:\transpeed:
# 1. "Claude outputs/" is a scratch/staging folder from earlier sessions —
#    old SQL migration drafts, duplicate component copies, unused logo
#    images. Harmless clutter EXCEPT for one file inside it:
#    "Claude outputs/env.local" (no leading dot, so the ".env*" rule above
#    does NOT catch it) holds a live RESEND_API_KEY plus the Supabase URL/
#    anon key in plain text. Without this line, that real secret would have
#    been committed and pushed to GitHub history the moment this folder
#    was added. Ignoring it here stops that; deleting the folder from disk
#    entirely (once device_bash is available again, or by hand in File
#    Explorer) is still the right long-term cleanup.
# 2. The client's raw working documents (Word docs, the architecture
#    pptx) aren't part of the website and don't belong in a code repo —
#    one of them ("Chat Bot.docx") has an open, unresolved question about
#    whether its content is meant to be confidential, which is reason
#    enough on its own to keep these out of git history rather than decide
#    that question by accident.
Claude outputs/
*.docx
*.pptx

# CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md — AI-assistant convention files (AGENTS.md is
# actually auto-written by `next dev` itself per its own comment; CLAUDE.md
# just points to it). Content's harmless either way, but the filenames
# alone are the kind of thing that shouldn't show up in the pushed repo
# (2026-09-15, per Vignesh: "it shouldn't be like the claude built it").
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
